# Prettier 3 reads .gitignore *as well as* this file — its --ignore-path defaults
# to both. (Prettier 2 did not; the older advice that "Prettier does not read
# .gitignore" no longer applies.) Verified on 3.8.1: a path listed only in
# .gitignore is skipped by `prettier --check .`.
#
# So entries here that are also gitignored are deliberate belt-and-braces. They
# survive an explicit --ignore-path, which some editor integrations set, and they
# state the intent where someone reading the formatting rules will find it. The
# entries that are NOT gitignored — the ADR-2 backend paths and docs/plans/ —
# are the ones doing load-bearing work, and each is proven so by removing it and
# watching the files reappear.

# Build and dependency output
node_modules/
build/
dist/
frontend/build/
frontend/dist/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Generated or bulk data — reformatting is churn
package-lock.json
backend/lambdas/package-lock.json
poets.json

# scripts/split-poets-json.js writes ~1,600 JSON files here, via
# JSON.stringify(…, null, 2) with no trailing newline — which Prettier always
# adds. Also gitignored, which is what actually excludes it today; kept here so
# the reason is recorded next to the other formatting exclusions.
output/

# Audit working sets are records; reformatting obscures what the auditors wrote.
# Gitignored by nothing, and every TRACKED file under docs/plans/ is covered here
# — `prettier --file-info` reports `ignored: true` for all of them — so by this
# file's own framing above, this entry is load-bearing. A remediation in progress
# adds untracked files under the same path, so the total number of files behind
# this entry varies by checkout; the tracked ones are what make it matter.
docs/plans/

# Local agent worktrees. Also gitignored.
.claude/

# ADR-2 reserves the backend's disposition for the user; no phase of this plan
# modifies these — and "modifies" includes reformatting. These are tracked files,
# so this entry is the only thing keeping them out: remove it and all five Lambda
# sources reappear in `--check`. backend/README.md and backend/scripts/deploy.sh
# are NOT on that list and stay inside the gate.
backend/lambdas/
backend/template.yaml
backend/samconfig.toml

# Generated by scripts/generate-search-index.mjs and shipped over the wire.
# Written on one line on purpose -- it is a machine-read asset, not a document
# anyone edits, and reformatting it would add ~30 kB of indentation to every
# visitor's download.
frontend/public/search-index.json
frontend/public/audio-dates.json
